This is already fixed on the current main/dev branches: commit 24de6cdf4 ("fix(api): Close cross-user and cross-tenant gaps", 2026-10-29) added the `user.is_superuser` check to `GET /api/v1/settings` in `cognee/api/v1/settings/routers/get_settings_router.py`, returning the same 403 shape the advisory suggests. The affected version (1.6.4, `f154b32a`) predates that commit. Current code:

```python
if not user.is_superuser:
    return JSONResponse(
        status_code=403,
        content={"error": "Superuser privileges required to read settings"},
    )
```

Nothing further to change.
